/-
This module provides a formalization of ray intersections in finite arithmetic, specifically focusing on the equivalence between modular equality and the existence of a linear decomposition. It defines `RayInter m r n` as `Nat.ModEq m n r` and proves key lemmas such as `modEq_iff_mod_eq` and `modEq_iff_exists_eq_mul_add`, culminating in `rayInter_iff_exists` which characterizes ray intersection by the existence of a multiplier `t` such that `n = m * t + r`.
-/

import Mathlib

set_option linter.mathlibStandardSet false

open scoped BigOperators
open scoped Real
open scoped Nat
open scoped Classical
open scoped Pointwise

set_option maxHeartbeats 0
set_option maxRecDepth 4000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 20000
